╭─ Issue description ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Issue Title: [Bug]: Content is always None when MCP server returns an 'error' to the client                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Description:                                                                                                                                    │
│ ## The bug                                                                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ In (https://github.com/dapr/dapr-agents/blob/main/dapr_agents/tool/mcp/client.py#L358-L366) the error handling from the                         │
│ `_process_tool_result()` always raises `ToolError` even though `content` _could_ hold a result output from the MCP server that we would like to │
│ re-iterate on:                                                                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│         # Handle error result                                                                                                                   │
│         if hasattr(result, 'isError') and result.isError:                                                                                       │
│             error_message = "Unknown error"                                                                                                     │
│             if hasattr(result, 'content') and result.content:                                                                                   │
│                 for content in result.content:                                                                                                  │
│                     if hasattr(content, 'text'):                                                                                                │
│                         error_message = content.text                                                                                            │
│                         break                                                                                                                   │
│             raise ToolError(f"MCP tool error: {error_message}")                                                                                 │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ This means that the return of `content` in                                                                                                      │
│ (https://github.com/dapr/dapr-agents/blob/main/dapr_agents/agent/patterns/toolcall/base.py#L106-L115) always yields `None` when                 │
│ `response.get_content()` is called and the mcp client threw a `ToolError`.                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ The solution is to not raise the `ToolError` if `hasattr(result, 'content') && hasattr(content, 'text')` evaluates true as we need this         │
│ `result.content.text`, even if it is an error from the MCP server, to feed it back to the model for next iteration:                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│         # Extract text content from result                                                                                                      │
│         if hasattr(result, 'content') and result.content:                                                                                       │
│             text_contents = []                                                                                                                  │
│             for content in result.content:                                                                                                      │
│                 if hasattr(content, 'text'):                                                                                                    │
│                     text_contents.append(content.text)                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│             # Return single string if only one content item                                                                                     │
│             logger.info(f"Tool result content: {text_contents}")                                                                                │
│             if len(text_contents) == 1:                                                                                                         │
│                 return text_contents[0]                                                                                                         │
│             elif text_contents:                                                                                                                 │
│                 return text_contents                                                                                                            │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│         if hasattr(result, 'isError') and result.isError:                                                                                       │
│             # Only triggered if the above didn't return with text_contents                                                                      │
│             raise ToolError(f"MCP tool error: {result}")                                                                                        │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ If we don't return the errors that may be thrown from the MCP server into `result.content.text`, the model will not get to learn from the       │
│ output of the MCP server and thus get stuck in a failure loop.                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
